# Normalise line endings in source, but never touch the released data.
#
# results/moment_decomposition_canonical/SHA256SUMS records a full-file sha256 of
# each CSV, and those CSVs are CRLF. The prereg records are hashed the same way.
# If git rewrote CRLF to LF on commit or back on checkout, every one of those
# hashes would change and validate_canonical_moments.py -- the blocking check the
# paper points readers at -- would fail on a fresh clone, for no reason a reader
# could diagnose. -text keeps the bytes exactly as released.

* text=auto

results/** -text
prereg/** -text
*.npz binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
